# Metro Garage Solutions — Web Performance

## Stack

- **Next.js 15.0.3** + **React 19 RC** — App Router, JavaScript (no TypeScript)
- **Single-page app** with hash sections: `#about`, `#services`, `#works`, `#contact`
- **Domain:** `https://metrogaragesolutions.com`

---

## Key Files

| Purpose | File |
|---------|------|
| Root layout | `src/app/layout.js` |
| Hero (video + LCP image) | `src/app/components/Hero.jsx` |
| Carousel (image gallery) | `src/app/components/Carousel.jsx` |
| Global styles | `src/app/globals.css` |
| Google Analytics | loaded via `@next/third-parties/google` in `layout.js` |

---

## What's Already Implemented

- `next/image` in Carousel — do not revert to raw `<img>`
- Adaptive video loading in Hero based on device type — preserve this pattern
- Fonts via `next/font/google` (Montserrat, Comfortaa, Rubik) — no render-blocking `@import`
- Google Analytics via `@next/third-parties/google` — production-gated on `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_TRACKING_ID`

**Do not duplicate or undo any of the above.**

---

## Priority Checks for This Project

### 1. Hero LCP (Critical)

The Hero component contains the page's LCP element. When editing it:

- The above-fold image or video poster must have `priority` set — never `loading="lazy"` on it
- Video should stay adaptive (mobile vs desktop) — do not flatten to a single source
- Verify the hero image has explicit `width`/`height` or a sized container to prevent CLS

### 2. Carousel Images (High)

- Every `next/image` in Carousel must have a correct `sizes` prop matching the CSS layout width
- Missing or wrong `sizes` causes the browser to download full-resolution images for thumbnails
- Example: `sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 33vw"`

### 3. Google Analytics Script (High)

- `@next/third-parties/google` already defers GA correctly — do not add a raw `<script>` tag alongside it
- If adding any other third-party script, use `next/script` with `strategy="lazyOnload"` or `"afterInteractive"`

### 4. Bundle Size (High)

- This is a JS-heavy single-page app; every new dependency counts
- Check bundle cost with `npx bundlephobia <package>` before installing
- Prefer direct imports over barrel imports (e.g., `lucide-react/dist/esm/icons/X` not `lucide-react`)

### 5. `"use client"` Placement (High)

- Keep `"use client"` on leaf interactive components only (buttons, form inputs, modals)
- Never add `"use client"` to layout-level components — it ships the whole subtree as client JS

---

## Project Conventions

**JavaScript, not TypeScript.** Use `.js` / `.jsx` extensions — no type annotations.

**No TypeScript-only patterns** — `React.memo`, hooks, and dynamic imports all work the same in JS.

**Dynamic imports for heavy components:**
```js
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';

const HeavyComponent = dynamic(() => import('./HeavyComponent'), {
  loading: () => <div className="skeleton" />,
});
// Only add ssr: false if the component uses browser-only APIs (window, canvas)
```

---

## Quick Audit Checklist

Before shipping any change that touches Hero, Carousel, or layout:

- [ ] Hero LCP image/video poster has `priority` (not `loading="lazy"`)
- [ ] All `next/image` instances have explicit `width`/`height` or a `fill` container with `aspectRatio`
- [ ] All `next/image` instances have a correct `sizes` prop
- [ ] No new `<img>` tags (use `next/image`)
- [ ] No new `<link href="fonts.googleapis.com">` (fonts are via `next/font`)
- [ ] No new raw `<script>` tags (use `next/script` with a `strategy`)
- [ ] `"use client"` is only on leaf components, not layouts or pages

